          %h2#terminology Terminology
          %p
            There are two inequivalent definitions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fr%C3%A9chet+spaces"} Fréchet spaces
            found in the literature. The original definition due to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Banach"} Stefan Banach
            defines
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fr%C3%A9chet+spaces"} Fréchet spaces
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metrizable+topological+space"} metrizable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+space"} complete
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+spaces"} topological vector spaces
          %p
            Later
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bourbaki"} Bourbaki
            (Topological vector spaces, Section II.4.1) added the condition of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+convex+vector+space"} local convexity
          %p The term “F-space” can refer to either of these definitions, although in the modern literature it is more commonly used to refer to the non-locally convex notion.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nLab"} nLab
            uses “F-space” to refer to the non-locally convex notion and “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fr%C3%A9chet+space"}> Fréchet space
            ” to refer to the locally convex notion.
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An
            %strong F-space
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+space"} topological vector space
            whose topology is induced by a complete F-norm.
          %p
            An
            %strong F-norm
            is a non-homogeneous variant of a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/norm"} norm
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric"} metric
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            that satisfies properties in between being a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-norm"} G-norm
            (on the underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            of the vector space) and being a norm. As with norms, there is a semi- variant.
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+field"} topological field
            (typically the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            or the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+ring"} topological ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative
            one); we will call the elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            = succeed "." do
              %em scalars
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            (or
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+over+a+ring"} module
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "." do
              %em vectors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \|{-}\|
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            from (the underlying set of)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            to the set of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
          #Gseminorm.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p If
            %ol
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %msub
                          %mn 0
                          %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|0_V\|} = 0
                (or even just
                = succeed ")," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mo ≤
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|0\|} \leq 0
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|{-x}\|} = {\|x\|}
                (or even just
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mo ≤
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|{-x}\|} \leq {\|x\|}
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi x
                        %mo +
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mo ≤
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mo +
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|x + y\|} \leq {\|x\|} + {\|y\|}
                for each vector
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                and vector
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
                (the
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangle+inequality"} triangle inequality
            %p
              then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
