            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+image"} essential image
            of that category within the category of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+spaces"} topological vector spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalently
            the category whose objects are F-spaces and whose morphisms are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous
            linear maps. (This is especially so with Fréchet spaces, which have a common alternative definition that makes no reference to a canonical metric.)
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            The usual examples of F-spaces that are not Fréchet spaces are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lebesgue+spaces"} Lebesgue spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi l
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l^p
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi p
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \lt p \lt 1
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-norm"} norm
            in which
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
